commit 0bb6e9a13cf18c3f1217aadf260d2d3553103a39

C03: a leading statement of what is open on the screen frames the request, and «ve qué hay en pantalla», «para ver la pantalla» and «identificá el botón» after a capture are the screen text read (SCREEN1807)

The strict reader now discards a screen-state preface («hay un diálogo de Steam abierto para instalar X, …», «there is a Steam dialog open; …») before reading the request, in the strict branch and in the authority gate, and the describe branch of the capture read accepts «ve qué hay en pantalla», «para ver la pantalla» and «identificá el botón»: the capture followed by ocr.read is the only faithful screen read on this PC (no vision provider).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


